Hmmm okay I hope you get your method working, but if you do what OcRam said, you don't need conditionals. You just need to build the id list based on the variable that tells who is alive. Like if you need to give the ids as a string, I think it's something like:
// you have troop with 3 members and an event self variable array, 0 killed, 1 alive, like [1,0,1]
const troop = $dataTroops[1].members;
let ids = "";
for (let i=0; i<troop.length; i++) {
if (this.getSelfVariableValue(mapId, eventId, varId)[i]) {
ids += troop[i].id.toString();
ids += ",";
}
}
Just add to the end there code to take away the final comma, I've no motivation to check how to do that LOL. But yeah, I think something like that should work.
